Z||000003||pHoOl||11-29-2001||01:53 PM||||I'm guessing that oversteer is when you steer, and the back end slides out.  Kinda like in a rwd car when you're going around a corner and hit the gas too hard??  I've been trying to figure out what understeer and oversteer is.  I know that fieros have understeer, and i know that when i take a corner too fast, or on wet pavement, the front tires slide instead of the back end swinging out.<P>Do i got it, or am i way off?  also, is it better to have understeer or oversteer?  I'd think that for your average driver, understeer so that you don't spin the car out, but for those of us who like to take corners fast and could do it with swinging out, i'm guessing oversteer would be better.<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||11-29-2001||07:38 PM||||under steer is when you turn the wheel and car doesnot turn as much as you thought it would.<BR>oversteer is when it turns more than you want it too.<BR>speeds and balance can cause a transition from under steer to oversteer by backing off gas or hiting brakes,as rearend comes out of line.<BR>to play without killing yourself get GPL demo<BR>SIM/game as it has best model of under/over steer and transitions. free demo at  <A HREF="http://www.papy.com/gpl/gpl.download.index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.papy.com/gpl/gpl.download.index.html</A>  get the 1.2 patch and the over 1.4 speed fix if your computer is over 1.4 MH speed on same site all free. may save you life!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||11-29-2001||07:46 PM||||ideally, you want the car 'neutral' where its just as much under as over steer. thats what you see race car drivers searching for in setups.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||11-30-2001||12:21 AM||||Oversteer is when you hit the *INSIDE* wall, and Understeer is when you hit the *OUTSIDE* wall  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Neutural is fast.  Neutural with a hint of oversteer (or understeer, selectable with throttle) is what you'll get in a properly setup car. (Fiero or other)<P>From the factory, they push.  Because people b****** at corvairs.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (and because it really is safer for idoits who shouldn't be given a licence anyway... but I digress!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
